## Documentation workflow (learning-first)

This is the **most important** part of the migration. For **every** file created or meaningfully edited:

1. Create or update `docs/<doc-name>.md` **in the same PR/commit slice** as the code change.
2. The doc must be **self-contained** — readable without opening the source file.
3. Write in **Korean** (code samples stay in English/TypeScript).
4. Do **not** batch all docs at the end; one doc per slice.

### Doc naming convention

Map source path → doc path under `docs/`:

| Source file | Doc file |
|-------------|----------|
| `src/atoms/theme.ts` | `docs/atoms-theme.md` |
| `src/atoms/auth.ts` | `docs/atoms-auth.md` |
| `src/lib/authActions.ts` | `docs/lib-authActions.md` |
| `src/components/AuthInitializer.tsx` | `docs/components-AuthInitializer.md` |
| `src/hooks/useTheme.ts` | `docs/hooks-useTheme.md` |
| `src/hooks/useAuth.ts` | `docs/hooks-useAuth.md` |
| `App.tsx` | `docs/App.md` |
| `package.json` (deps slice) | `docs/package-jotai-deps.md` |

Pattern: `docs/<folder>-<filename>.md` (drop `src/` prefix, use kebab-case).

### Required sections in every doc

Each `docs/*.md` must include:

1. **이 파일의 역할** — one paragraph, what problem it solves
2. **Jotai 개념** — which primitives are used (`atom`, `atomWithStorage`, derived atom, `useAtom`, `useSetAtom`, `useAtomValue`, `Provider`)
3. **Before → After** — what Context/store pattern existed and what changed
4. **코드 walkthrough** — block-by-block explanation of the final file
5. **다른 파일과의 관계** — imports, who reads/writes these atoms
6. **흔한 실수** — 2–3 pitfalls specific to this file (e.g. stale closure, missing Provider, AsyncStorage race)
7. **직접 해보기** — one small exercise (e.g. “add a `isDarkAtom` derived atom”)

### Agent / developer checklist per slice

- [ ] Doc file exists and matches the code in the same slice
- [ ] Doc explains **why**, not only **what**
- [ ] No server-state logic moved into Jotai
- [ ] `npm run typecheck` or equivalent passes (when script exists)
- [ ] Manual smoke: theme switch, login, logout, deep-link auth (Auth slices)

